{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1143728-warding-circle-versus-lupines-in-the-umbra","id":1143728,"title":"Warding Circle Versus Lupines in the UMBRA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-25T04:21:35-07:00","id":1143728,"title":"Warding Circle Versus Lupines in the UMBRA","content":"Hi!<br /> The Tremere vampires have the ritual <b>Warding Circle Versus Ghouls </b>with the following wording:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Warding Circle Versus Ghouls</b><br /> This ritual is enacted in a manner similar to that of Ward versus Ghouls, but creates a circle centered on the caster into which a ghoul cannot pass without being burned. The circle may be made as large and as permanent as the caster desires, so long as she is willing to pay the necessary price. Many Tremere chantries and havens are protected by this and other Warding Circle rituals. System: The ritual requires three blood points of mortal blood. The caster determines the size of the warding circle when it is cast; the default radius is 10 feet and every 10-foot increase raises the difficulty by one, to a maximum of 9 (one additional success is required for every 10-foot increase past the number necessaryto raise the difficulty to 9). The player spends one blood point for every 10 feet of radius and rolls. The ritual takes the normal casting time if it is to be temporary (lasting for the rest of the night) or one night if it is to be permanent (lasting a year and a day). Once the warding circle is established, any ghoul who attempts to cross its boundary feels a tingle on his skin and a slight breeze on his face - a successful Intelligence + Occult roll (difficulty 8) identifies this as a warding circle. If the ghoul attempts to press on, he must roll more successes on a willpower roll (difficulty of the caster's Thaumaturgy rating + 3) than the caster rolled when establishing the ward. Failure indicates that the ward blocks his passage and inflicts three dice of bashing damage on him, and his next roll to attempt to enter the circle is at +1 difficulty. If the ghoul leaves the circle and attempts to enter it again, he must repeat the roll. Attempts to leave the circle are not blocked.</i><br /> <br /> How do you think this will affect the penumbra? Just making the same rolls? A guardian spirit attacking the Garous? No effect on the Penumbra?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T04:54:50-07:00","id":1143740,"title":"","content":"I think older writeups of Ward vs Lupines includes silvers so I'd make the same rolls... and make them agg damage since Garou pretty much laugh at bashing and lethal. I don't see why it would change in the umbra especially wince ward and warding circle vs Spirit exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T07:59:02-07:00","id":1143787,"title":"","content":"One should use a ruling that makes the ward something useful, otherwise no one would bother making them. Warding Circle vs Spirits doesn't target the Umbra explicitly , but it has to in order to do it's job, same goes for the one about Garou. A Warding circle vs Garou that doesn't affect the Umbra would be woefully uneffective. I think it's better to assume that all wards just work in both sides of the Gauntlet/Shroud, incidentally this would allow a Ward vs Vampires to block astral travelers using Auspex.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't care about the type of damage, the real gain it's to keep the thing out, the damage it's a bonus that adds to that purpose. In my opinion the +1 penalty for failure in successive attempts weighs much more than the damage to the end result even for ghouls or vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-25-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T09:33:15-07:00","id":1143816,"title":"","content":"So echoing above, just have the Wards affect the Umbra. Vampire barely acknowledges the spirit worlds so you never really get clarifications for them. And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said, the Willpower roll is the big thing. The damage isn't (even if it were Agg, Garou would scoff at the damage). I see no reason to upgrade the damage to Agg.<br /> <br /> In prior editions the Wards were completely pathetic. Now at least they might be unpassable based on the Willpower roll adjustment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Why are there so many Garou/Tremere threads lately?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-25-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T09:53:08-07:00","id":1143825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1143728-warding-circle-versus-lupines-in-the-umbra?p=1143816#post1143816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Why are there so many Garou/Tremere threads lately?</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Last two, because my Garou PC are about to assault an Tremere-ish haven.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I don't know about the other, but Garous have a reputation for killing everybody around, except what really matters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\