is an excuse to allow anything) to accomplish a higher rating. Just that it won't happen merely as a side effect to the Tremere being there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For some reason I thought places of the wyrm had higher Gauntlet ratings for Gaian Garou like how Ananasi have different dififculities because of their connection to the weaver.. but I can't find that in the books so my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T05:28:57-07:00","id":1144715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1143728-warding-circle-versus-lupines-in-the-umbra?p=1144096#post1144096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. Also, remember that most Tremere thaumaturges have zero knowledge of the Umbra, the war of the Triat of any Garou cosmology. The various Spirit oriented Paths are rare in the Pyramid. For the most part, Tremere worry about fighting other Vampires, who are their main enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and I don't. The point in regards to most Tremere having little knowledge of the War of the Triat and Garou seems very fair. But I'm not quite so sure in regards to Umbral knowledge. Given the access of Auspex to Tremere as well. And I've never seen language that spirit oriented Paths are any rarer than other secondary Paths. While Path of Blood is said to be the primary in most cases, is there actual fluff that stuff like Spirit Manipulation and Elemental Mastery are more uncommon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T07:07:08-07:00","id":1144750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1143728-warding-circle-versus-lupines-in-the-umbra?p=1144649#post1144649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For some reason I thought places of the wyrm had higher Gauntlet ratings for Gaian Garou like how Ananasi have different dififculities because of their connection to the weaver.. but I can't find that in the books so my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. It's just set up so that Weaver influence is what causes the higher Gauntlet ratings. Wyld and Wyrm have little to do with it. For the Ananasi, the heavier Weaver influence still leads to a higher Gauntlet. They just use that to their advantage for stepping sideways. Any other power based on a Gauntlet rating is still going to be higher difficulty.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:16:39-07:00","id":1144781,"title":"","content":"An interesting observation vis-a-vis Kindred knowledge of Garou stuff. Generally speaking the genre assumptions of the books seem to be that even studied Kindred occultists don't really get into Umbral shit. Generally I agree with this, just because I prefer not mixing my cosmologies and my themes. At the same time though I've played in several long running, large player base LARPs over the years, and while the genre-bending that often goes on in them can be pretty cringe-inducing I also think they can offer some constructive lessons in how certain game assumptions actually hold up to the stress test. In this case what I have repeatedly noticed is that Kindred knowledge of Garou and Umbra lore is directly related to how much of a threat the Garou are or have been in the game. It only takes one or two terrifying Garou attacks where they put all their outside context bullshit on display for people to realize that knowing how to deal with it is necessary for their survival. The more contact that Kindred have with Garou, the more likely it is for Spirit Manipulation and similar things to proliferate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T09:22:12-07:00","id":1144807,"title":"","content":"Knowledge it's something relative.<br /> <br /> There's a gap between knowing that there's this shadow world next to ours where spirit live, <i>and to know that Garou can travel there</i>. Just like there's a world of difference between knowing vampires exist, and knowing what powers they have (movies may give an idea, but movies are often wrong. The Garou that *knows* vampires can put you in a trance because movies should be sure to carry a lot of garlic to fend agains that...in the same vein, vampires carrying silver, because movies, should feel very sure in a moonless night, after all, Garou can only shapeshift at full moon).<br /> <br /> Every Tremere that's not a total newbie and many vampires may know that the shadow world and spirits do exist, but there's a huge gap between *that* and knowing about Umbral Layers, Realms, Spirit Hosts. There's a world to learn before said Tremere can start to understand Umbral politics to heavily use spirits to it's advantage without risking to anger *beings* that it's better not to anger. Just like knowing that vampires exist and having an idea about common powers and weaknesses doesn't make you able to understand kindred politics.<br /> <br /> That being said, to assure your ward stops things on both sides of the barrier you don't need to be an expert. Knowing that the spirit world it's there and that the barrier can be traversed it's enough. That's not a whole lot of Umbral lore. And I think we can assume that the Tremere that invented the Warding Circle vs Lupines knew one or two things about their capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-28-2017, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T16:22:17-07:00","id":1490197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1143728-warding-circle-versus-lupines-in-the-umbra?p=1144715#post1144715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree and I don't. The point in regards to most Tremere having little knowledge of the War of the Triat and Garou seems very fair. But I'm not quite so sure in regards to Umbral knowledge. Given the access of Auspex to Tremere as well. And I've never seen language that spirit oriented Paths are any rarer than other secondary Paths. While Path of Blood is said to be the primary in most cases, is there actual fluff that stuff like Spirit Manipulation and Elemental Mastery are more uncommon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elemental Mastery just lets you manipulate physical substances and summon elementals and is a hold over from old Order of Hermes techniques. Spirit Manipulation is a rare Path. I know that in that 90s LARP I played in, the local Tremere were utterly unequipped to handle our use of the Umbra. The only aspect of the city they had on their side were the humans - we had everything else that wasn't the Wyrm. The Manhattan City Father saw the leeches are wyrm parasites, and knew most of their plans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}